{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining focused recovery tests pass. I found two additional receipt-boundary failures in source: recovery can create a second run when a dispatch run exists without its receipt, and it refuses to clear a stalled marker when the receipt is already present. I’m assembling the required draft with those defects and the stale-claim takeover race, then I’ll run the native draft preflight and correct anything it rejects."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 105,\n      \"summary\": \"Stale release takeover is not exclusive across the rename-and-republish window. A second taker that read the old claim can rename a first taker'\"'s newly published live claim, then fail its byte check; another cancel can publish a fresh claim and enter the release body concurrently, creating duplicate failed runs and racing the receipt.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 152,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"If a process stops after publishing the attempt receipt but before removing the stalled marker, retrying cancel exits at the existing-receipt check and never clears the marker. The attempt remains shown as stalled and cannot be repaired through the advertised cancel path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 199,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Recovery recognizes only an earlier abandonment run. If dispatch recorded its ordinary run but stopped before publishing the attempt receipt, cancel ignores that run and records a second abandonment run for the same attempt, corrupting the attempt's run history instead of completing the receipt from the existing result.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:77-115,167-183; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:263-303; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1126-1133; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:263-303; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:101-114 still uses os.Rename on the canonical claim without binding the rename to the bytes/inode previously read; the passing TestAStaleClaimHasOneTaker at pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:378-410 does not force the interleaving described in N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:189-197,226-233; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:414-441; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept R1-R6, D1-D2 and L1-L4; reviewed process matching, pidfd signaling, baseline handling, dispatch ordering, attempt/run/receipt accounting, release ownership and crash boundaries, CLI list/cancel projections, brief versioning, English and Portuguese manuals, and scaffold copies. Ran focused tests and vet, plus the planned POSE checks; global and module validation could not write Go build/cache state in the read-only sandbox.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified the exact sealed-checkout marker and pidfd recheck for visible processes, and the baseline distinction for unreadable same-user processes. The unresolved assumptions are that descendants retain the environment marker and Linux /proc remains inspectable. L1 (a descendant that clears the marker), L2 (non-Linux group-only termination), L3 (pre-existing opaque processes are disclosed; newly opaque processes fail cleanup), and L4 (markerless earlier-engine reservations rely on explicit operator confirmation) are stated residual risks, not hidden guarantees.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The stale-claim takeover can expose two release bodies to the same attempt. The receipt and post-receipt recovery boundaries in N2 and N3 also remain incomplete.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI adds an optional cancel flag and stalled-cause projection; persisted run and receipt schemas are unchanged. The affected delegate surface has sealed integration evidence.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt IDs are validated before path use; incomplete or unreadable histories and receipts fail closed with actionable diagnostics. The focused recovery tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds no REST, MCP, event, or provider contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are existing /admin/refresh, /healthz, and /mcp declarations, outside these changed boundaries.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ended processes and pre-existing opaque processes are named in safety.limitations; failures identify scan, pin, signal, receipt, and history problems. The stalled listing includes a cause and release command.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI addition is opt-in, prior ledger schemas remain unchanged, and prior template versions remain addressable. The English and Brazilian Portuguese manuals and embedded copies were updated.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ordinary dispatch result can already exist when receipt publication fails; recovery then appends a second abandonment run rather than completing the attempt from that result. N2 also leaves a stale marker after the receipt is present.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the original cause: a session-escaped command misses process-group termination, so Linux scans for the run-specific sealed-checkout value and pins the PID before signaling. D2 addresses interrupted reservations by retaining the reservation and writing failed-run/receipt records after proof of abandonment; R5 motivates the explicit-confirmation path for markerless earlier-engine records. The selected causes and evidence align, though the implementation recovery defects are reported separately.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The manual, locale copy, and scaffold copies describe Linux-only matching, limitations, reviewer command completion, and the new cancel flow. The brief uses immutable template /10 and its digest was updated.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"After receipt publication followed by interruption, cancel reports an existing receipt but leaves the attempt permanently displayed as stalled.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed unit suite covers R1/R2/R4 process cleanup, R3 brief text, and R5/R6 interrupted dispatch and release. The focused tests for dispatch reaping, abandoned attempts, live-owner refusal, and brief behavior passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation is within the approved pose-mcp dispatch/ledger/CLI/template scope and synchronized manuals/scaffold copies; no unrelated public API or storage schema change was introduced.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Termination is limited to a process carrying this run's checkout value and the signal is sent through a pidfd after rechecking. Visible live owners cannot be released; the weaker markerless path requires explicit operator confirmation and is disclosed as L4.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The smallest sufficient process fix is a run-specific marker scan with pidfd validation; a broad user-wide kill or new cgroup system would exceed the stated need. The smallest recovery alternative is one exclusive per-attempt claim plus retained records, not ledger deletion or a generalized recovery framework. Environment clearing and non-Linux behavior are explicitly excluded; an atomic stale-claim takeover is necessary to preserve the selected design and is the remaining defect in N1.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran through the sealed CLI and exited 0. It printed many orphan-path warnings because the resolved change-set range includes unrelated work; I did not treat those out-of-scope paths as subject defects.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran --json; the observed design report had no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence. It reported three pre-existing unobserved HTTP consumers; none is changed by this subject.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command ran but reported an incomplete scan because two unrelated specs have invalid scope metadata, plus one uncovered marker; these are not in changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Its precondition is a completed attestation. The brief prohibits recording an attestation, so this completion-only check cannot run in this review.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Its precondition is a completed attestation. The brief prohibits recording an attestation, so this completion-only check cannot run in this review.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran and selected the backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules used for this review.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran --strict: one target, 236 results, zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required strict run was attempted but its checks could not create Go build directories or update the read-only build cache. The sealed bundle contains passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence for this subject; focused tests and vet also passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required strict module run was attempted but all Go checks failed before execution on read-only build/cache writes. The sealed bundle contains passing pose-mcp build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and vet also passed.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 105,\n      \"summary\": \"Stale release takeover is not exclusive across the rename-and-republish window. A second taker that read the old claim can rename a first taker'\"'s newly published live claim, then fail its byte check; another cancel can publish a fresh claim and enter the release body concurrently, creating duplicate failed runs and racing the receipt.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 152,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"If a process stops after publishing the attempt receipt but before removing the stalled marker, retrying cancel exits at the existing-receipt check and never clears the marker. The attempt remains shown as stalled and cannot be repaired through the advertised cancel path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 199,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Recovery recognizes only an earlier abandonment run. If dispatch recorded its ordinary run but stopped before publishing the attempt receipt, cancel ignores that run and records a second abandonment run for the same attempt, corrupting the attempt's run history instead of completing the receipt from the existing result.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:77-115,167-183; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:263-303; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1126-1133; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:263-303; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:101-114 still uses os.Rename on the canonical claim without binding the rename to the bytes/inode previously read; the passing TestAStaleClaimHasOneTaker at pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:378-410 does not force the interleaving described in N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:189-197,226-233; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:414-441; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'StaleClaim|InterruptedRelease|IncompleteRunHistory|MarkerlessReservation|InterruptedDispatch|AbandonedAttempt' (pass)\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept R1-R6, D1-D2 and L1-L4; reviewed process matching, pidfd signaling, baseline handling, dispatch ordering, attempt/run/receipt accounting, release ownership and crash boundaries, CLI list/cancel projections, brief versioning, English and Portuguese manuals, and scaffold copies. Ran focused tests and vet, plus the planned POSE checks; global and module validation could not write Go build/cache state in the read-only sandbox.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a5ef137330d83b73\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified the exact sealed-checkout marker and pidfd recheck for visible processes, and the baseline distinction for unreadable same-user processes. The unresolved assumptions are that descendants retain the environment marker and Linux /proc remains inspectable. L1 (a descendant that clears the marker), L2 (non-Linux group-only termination), L3 (pre-existing opaque processes are disclosed; newly opaque processes fail cleanup), and L4 (markerless earlier-engine reservations rely on explicit operator confirmation) are stated residual risks, not hidden guarantees.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The stale-claim takeover can expose two release bodies to the same attempt. The receipt and post-receipt recovery boundaries in N2 and N3 also remain incomplete.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI adds an optional cancel flag and stalled-cause projection; persisted run and receipt schemas are unchanged. The affected delegate surface has sealed integration evidence.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt IDs are validated before path use; incomplete or unreadable histories and receipts fail closed with actionable diagnostics